### Detailed Module Breakdown (Active Scaffolding)

- **`api/`**: Handles the transport layer logic (FastAPI routers, versioned endpoints under `api/v1/`, status codes, query/path parameters, and HTTP-level dependencies). It must never contain business rules, SQL queries, or direct LLM calls.
- **`core/`**: Houses application-wide utilities such as environment configuration, JSON-structured logging, global error handlers, and middleware. Do not use it as a dumping ground for unowned code.
- **`schemas/`**: Contains Pydantic models for request payloads and response serialization at the HTTP boundary. These are transport contracts, not persistence or domain models.
- **`services/`**: Implements application use cases. It coordinates domain logic, data access, and external integrations, acting as the primary orchestrator between API endpoints and infrastructure.
{%- if include_db %}
- **`db/`**: Owns database engines, connection pools, ORM session configuration (`async_sessionmaker`), and database persistence models. Keep driver-specific details and connection lifecycles here.
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_domain %}
- **`domain/`**: Encapsulates pure business logic, entities, value objects, and domain invariants. It must remain entirely agnostic of frameworks (FastAPI, Pydantic, SQLAlchemy) and external infrastructure.
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_repositories %}
- **`repositories/`**: Implements data access contracts and repository patterns, shielding application services from direct query-building and ORM specifics.
{%- endif %}
